<wpf:ResourceDictionary xml:space="preserve" xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml" xmlns:s="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib" xmlns:ss="urn:shemas-jetbrains-com:settings-storage-xaml" xmlns:wpf="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation">
	<!-- Named arguments are a deliberate prose-parameter documentation convention (GRAMMAR §10:
	     from:, to:, description:). Protecting them takes TWO settings, because inspect and cleanup
	     read different axes and do not share a switch.

	     1. The inspection severities below stop the IDE and inspectcode REPORTING a deliberate name
	        as removable. They have no effect on cleanup: cleanup overrides the severity of every
	        rule its enabled modules need, so DO_NOT_SHOW cannot reach it.
	     2. The cleanup profile below stops cleanup REWRITING it. "Arrange argument style" is the
	        cleanup task that normalises arguments to positional, and turning it off is the only way
	        to leave argument style as-authored — the style setting itself is binary (positional or
	        named) with no "leave alone" value.

	     Contributors need not run ReSharper; the file is simply ignored by anything that doesn't. -->
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=ArgumentsStyleLiteral/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=ArgumentsStyleStringLiteral/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=ArgumentsStyleNamedExpression/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=ArgumentsStyleOther/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=ArgumentsStyleAnonymousFunction/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>

	<!-- The cleanup profile: "Built-in: Full Cleanup" with one task off, ArrangeArgumentsStyle.

	     A profile is a single XML-encoded blob under /Default/CodeStyle/CodeCleanup/Profiles/=<Name>/,
	     and it is NOT a diff against a built-in: any task the blob omits reads back as the
	     descriptor's default, which is off. So this enumerates every C# cleanup task Full Cleanup
	     turns on. The list was read off ReSharper 2026.1.2's own cleanup modules, not guessed —
	     re-derive it on a ReSharper upgrade (CodeStylesCleanupModule.ALL_CODE_STYLES and the
	     SetDefaultSetting(FULL) arm of each ICodeCleanupModule). A task JetBrains adds later will
	     be missing here and silently not run; a missing task is a nicety not applied, never a
	     rewrite of code you meant to keep.

	     Three tasks are False deliberately, and each one is load-bearing:

	     - ArrangeArgumentsStyle, per the named-argument note above.
	     - CSReorderTypeMembers, because reordering is the only task that moves a member wholesale
	       across a file, and several files here pin line numbers. SpecValidationSpecs.cs is the
	       sharp case: forty expected messages in SpecValidationTests.cs quote its anchors as
	       literal "SpecValidationSpecs.cs:N" text, so one hoisted member silently moves forty
	       assertions. Member order is a nicety; a line-pinned golden is not. Leaving it off is what
	       lets any file in the repo be passed to cleanup without first consulting a list.
	     - CSUpdateFileHeader, which Full Cleanup leaves off too.

	     The trailing newline at EOF is NOT settable here — insert_final_newline is an .editorconfig
	     standard property with no .DotSettings equivalent. The repo carries a two-line .editorconfig
	     for exactly that one knob, and that is where to change it. -->
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeStyle/CodeCleanup/Profiles/=LoadBearing_003A_0020Full_0020Cleanup_0020_0028keep_0020named_0020arguments_0029/@EntryIndexedValue">&lt;?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-16"?&gt;&lt;Profile name="LoadBearing: Full Cleanup (keep named arguments)"&gt;&lt;CSReformatCode&gt;True&lt;/CSReformatCode&gt;&lt;CSharpFormatDocComments&gt;True&lt;/CSharpFormatDocComments&gt;&lt;CSharpReformatComments&gt;True&lt;/CSharpReformatComments&gt;&lt;CSOptimizeUsings&gt;&lt;OptimizeUsings&gt;True&lt;/OptimizeUsings&gt;&lt;EmbraceInRegion&gt;False&lt;/EmbraceInRegion&gt;&lt;RegionName&gt;&lt;/RegionName&gt;&lt;/CSOptimizeUsings&gt;&lt;CSShortenReferences&gt;True&lt;/CSShortenReferences&gt;&lt;CSReorderTypeMembers&gt;False&lt;/CSReorderTypeMembers&gt;&lt;CSUpdateFileHeader&gt;False&lt;/CSUpdateFileHeader&gt;&lt;RemoveCodeRedundancies&gt;True&lt;/RemoveCodeRedundancies&gt;&lt;CSUseAutoProperty&gt;True&lt;/CSUseAutoProperty&gt;&lt;CSMakeFieldReadonly&gt;True&lt;/CSMakeFieldReadonly&gt;&lt;CSMakeAutoPropertyGetOnly&gt;True&lt;/CSMakeAutoPropertyGetOnly&gt;&lt;CSArrangeQualifiers&gt;True&lt;/CSArrangeQualifiers&gt;&lt;CSFixBuiltinTypeReferences&gt;True&lt;/CSFixBuiltinTypeReferences&gt;&lt;CSCodeStyleAttributes ArrangeVarStyle="True" ArrangeTypeAccessModifier="True" ArrangeTypeMemberAccessModifier="True" SortModifiers="True" ArrangeAccessors="True" ArrangeArgumentsStyle="False" RemoveRedundantParentheses="True" AddMissingParentheses="True" ArrangeBraces="True" ArrangeAttributes="True" ArrangeCodeBodyStyle="True" ArrangeTrailingCommas="True" ArrangeObjectCreation="True" ArrangeDefaultValue="True" ArrangeEmptyString="True" ArrangeNamespaces="True" ArrangeNullCheckingPattern="True" /&gt;&lt;/Profile&gt;</s:String>

	<!-- ReSharper's "profile to use when nobody picks one".

	     A runner that honours this key reads it before cleaning, so a cleanup call naming no
	     profile still gets the profile above and the deliberate named arguments survive. Omitting
	     the profile argument is the intended path there; naming it is merely harmless.

	     Bare `jb cleanupcode` never reads this key: jb always defaults to Full Cleanup, so a direct
	     CLI run must still pass the profile by name. jb's switch for that is not spelled literally
	     here: XML forbids adjacent hyphens inside a comment, and one such spelling once left this
	     file unreadable to every conformant XML parser while jb itself carried on regardless.
	     DotSettingsCleanupProfileTests pins the file well-formed. -->
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeStyle/CodeCleanup/SilentCleanupProfile/@EntryValue">LoadBearing: Full Cleanup (keep named arguments)</s:String>

	<!-- Line wrapping is deliberately OFF, and this key is what pins it.

	     Fluent chains here follow the LINQ chain convention: one call per line, leading dot (see
	     McpResultAssertions.cs). The test project got that shape in one machine pass, under a
	     temporary WRAP_CHAINED_METHOD_CALLS=CHOP_ALWAYS key removed in the same commit that
	     landed the reformat. The formatter's standing job is to PRESERVE the shape (keep existing
	     line breaks), never to compute it, and the key above is what holds wrapping to that job.

	     Two places were held out of the pass and are why no wrapping key may stand here:
	     SpecValidationSpecs.cs, whose forty expected messages in SpecValidationTests.cs quote its
	     anchors as literal "SpecValidationSpecs.cs:N" text, and the Fixtures and Stubs trees, whose
	     goldens pin their line numbers. A chain-wrap key left in place chops them on the next
	     cleanup of any file, silently. Margin wrapping is the same hazard from the other side: it
	     fully chops any chain that already carries one break. Wrapping off is what keeps "any file
	     can be passed to cleanup" true. Chop new chains by hand; cleanup will keep them.

	     DotSettingsCleanupProfileTests pins both halves: this entry present and False, and no entry
	     anywhere in the file whose key names chained method calls. -->
	<s:Boolean x:Key="/Default/CodeStyle/CodeFormatting/CSharpFormat/WRAP_LINES/@EntryValue">False</s:Boolean>
	<s:Boolean x:Key="/Default/Environment/SettingsMigration/IsMigratorApplied/=JetBrains_002EReSharper_002EPsi_002ECSharp_002ECodeStyle_002ECSharpKeepExistingMigration/@EntryIndexedValue">True</s:Boolean>
	<s:Boolean x:Key="/Default/Environment/SettingsMigration/IsMigratorApplied/=JetBrains_002EReSharper_002EPsi_002ECSharp_002ECodeStyle_002ECSharpPlaceEmbeddedOnSameLineMigration/@EntryIndexedValue">True</s:Boolean>
	<s:Boolean x:Key="/Default/Environment/SettingsMigration/IsMigratorApplied/=JetBrains_002EReSharper_002EPsi_002ECSharp_002ECodeStyle_002ECSharpUseContinuousIndentInsideBracesMigration/@EntryIndexedValue">True</s:Boolean>
	<s:Boolean x:Key="/Default/Environment/SettingsMigration/IsMigratorApplied/=JetBrains_002EReSharper_002EPsi_002ECSharp_002ECodeStyle_002ESettingsUpgrade_002EMigrateBlankLinesAroundFieldToBlankLinesAroundProperty/@EntryIndexedValue">True</s:Boolean>
</wpf:ResourceDictionary>
